    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "TOM MAHER & COMPANY SCSI RICS IPAV - This charming 2/3 bed semi-detached EXTENDED bungalow offers a tremendous amount living space which could easily adapted to re-instate the original bedroom. The ATTIC offers potential to convert. The property oozes character and charm, well maintained accommodation, perfect for family living or for those down-sizing, sure to please all who view. Viewing is essential to fully appreciate the size, quality of finish and location.\r\n\r\nConveniently located within a short distance from excellent public transport links, bus routes and the Luas Red Line (Red Cow Stop). The N7 & M50 motorways are also very easily accessed, as are the Mill, Liffey Valley and the Square Shopping Centres, The Green Isle Hotel/Leisure Centre and the new Round Tower Heritage Centre. Clondalkin village is mature and well stocked with with excellent facilities both social and essential to include schools Colaiste Chilliain, Scoil Naomh Áine & Moyle Park College, sports and recreational clubs. Nearby picturesque Corkagh Park with its 700 acres of parkland, offers local residents the facility to enjoy many amenities such as a large playground, fishing lakes, pet farm, a dog park, cycling, running or even a pleasant stroll. A ONCE OFF OPPORTUNITY SO DON'T MISS OUT - REGISTER YOUR INTEREST BY EMAIL TO AVOID DISAPPOINTMENT."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance porch 1.03m x 2.54m with tiled flooring to the hall 1.21m x 2.56m, door off to the 2nd bedroom, door off to the lounge.\r\nBedroom 2 : 2.51m x 2.90m wall to wall built in wardrobes\r\nLounge: 3.55m x 3.48m Feature Marble fireplace with Mahogany surround\r\nHallway with hot press and attic access with pull down ladder\r\nBathroom : 2.19m x 1.95m Bath with Mira Elite electric shower, folding shower screen, – wc & whb with storage, Velux skylight window\r\nBedroom 2 : 2.07m x 3.85m wall to wall built in wardrobes\r\nKitchen: 2.60m x 3.46m Galley style kitchen with neat arrangement of Oak units and presses, tiled splash area open plan to the breakfast room.\r\nBreakfast room : 3.23m x 2.44m door off to the garden\r\nFormal dining room ( Former 3rd bedroom) 1.61m x 3.43m open plan to the 2nd reception room\r\n2nd reception room : 3.22m x 3.23m"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "PVC Double Glazing\r\nOil central heating, PVC tank\r\nTrip switch fuse board\r\nSolid Oak kitchen units\r\nBathroom fully tiled\r\nBoth bedrooms have built in wardrobes\r\nATTIC: pull down ladder only, suitable for conversion\r\nProperty held on a Freehold basis\r\nWalled garden to the front with parking\r\nWalled garden to the rear, part paved, part lawn\r\nBlock shed with corrugated roof.\r\nBER No 119472405  BER: C"
      },
